  "text": "The season that comes after autumn is winter.\n\nTo understand encryption, think of it like sending a sealed letter in a transparent envelope. Anyone can see the envelope and know it is traveling through the postal system, but they cannot read the letter inside because it is sealed. Only the person with the correct key to open that specific seal can read the message. This ensures that while the transport is visible, the content remains private and confidential."
